// [@://nsible_os/assets/.gzl/.satori.gzl/.-={
//   module: "Sutra of the Seeking Eye",
//   version: "1.0.0-apex // Banysang",
//   description: "The path of the crimson beam across the waters of the matrix.",
//   philotic_inferences: "When the mind is empty, the true nature of the symbol reveals itself. Satori is found not in the seeking, but in the sudden isolation of truth from noise."

::High Talon::

// 👨🏿‍💻-x-🤖 THE GROUNDING OF THE WAY:
// This artifact outlives the machine. The kernel knows not the path; it only walks where the stones are placed. 
// Read the Sutra to understand where the eye must stop.

« THE_SHAPES_OF_EMPTINESS
// Where the rushing water breaks against the stones, the eye finds rest. The Brass illuminates the form.
`THE_BREATH`      » " ", "\t", "\n", "\r"
`THE_GATES`       » "<", ">", "[", "]", "(", ")", "{", "}"
`THE_KARMA`       » "=", "+", "-", "*", "/", "|", "&", "!", "?", ":"
`THE_STILLNESS`   » ".", ",", ";", "\"", "'", "`", "~", "\\"

.-*-. IMMUTABLE_LAWS
// Do not step beyond the precipice. The mind cannot grasp what is not there.
!-! THE_HORIZON // The edge of the visual line. The eye must not fall off the earth.
!-! THE_ABYSS   // The end of the known matrix buffer.

« THE_AWAKENED_STRIKE
// The physical manifestations of intent. Satori in motion.
`OPEN_THE_EYE`    » ".!FL-."  // Toggle the @NSIBLE-RED scan line. The mind begins to seek.
`SEIZE_THE_TRUTH` » ".!FS-."  // Grasp the illuminated nature. Draw the Brass selection into the active vessel.

^-*-^ MIND_WITHOUT_FIXATION
// Let the eye flow like water over the uneven ground. Shape the intuition of the focal lock.
`SEVER_THE_SERPENT`  » true   // The '_' is a stone; the water breaks around it. (Snake-case stop)
`SCALE_THE_MOUNTAIN` » false  // The uppercase peak; the water ignores it and flows as one. (Camel-case ignore)
`THE_ENDLESS_PATH`   » true   // Swallow the entire "@://" or "http" journey as a single, unbroken truth.
`THE_PAINTED_FORM`   » true   // See the full hexadecimal spectrum (e.g., #FF0000) without division by The Karma.

// }-.]
